{"duration_api_ms":4649,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c133ce6d-adae-42ed-9002-791b1ed51aa5","total_cost_usd":0.012237600000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":625,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":625,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":355,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":625,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":625},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1191,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0001296,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":355,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":625,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.012108,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":14,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":625,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Authorized Participants (APs)** operate in the **primary market**. They are typically large broker-dealers with contractual agreements with the ETF issuer, and they alone can **create or redeem ETF shares** directly with the fund, usually in large blocks (\"creation units,\" often 10,000–50,000 shares) exchanged for baskets of securities or cash. This arbitrage mechanism keeps the ETF's price close to its NAV.\n\n**Market makers** operate in the **secondary market** (exchanges). They continuously post **bid and ask quotes**, providing liquidity so investors can trade ETF shares intraday. They profit from spreads and hedge their inventory. Designated **Lead Market Makers** have formal quoting obligations on exchanges.\n\n**Key overlap:** Many firms (e.g., Jane Street, Citadel Securities, Virtu) act as both. Market makers that aren't APs route creation/redemption orders through an AP.\n\n**In short:** APs manage ETF *supply*; market makers manage *tradability*.","ttft_ms":1020,"type":"result","duration_ms":4134,"uuid":"b8a6c814-f7c2-429b-a442-da7d6867b569","ttft_stream_ms":972,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":972,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
